==English==
[[File:Scallion.jpg|thumb|A bundle of ''scallions'' (spring onions, ''Allium fistulosum'').]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|scullion}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|scalon}}, from {{der|en|xno|scalun}} (variant of {{cog|fro|eschaloigne}}), from a Proto-Romance derivation of {{der|en|VL.|*escalonia}}, from {{der|en|la|Ascalonius}} (in ''{{m|la|caepa|t=onion}} Ascalonius'', "shallot"), from {{m|la|Ascalo|t=Ascalon}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἀσκάλων|t={{w|Ashkelon|Ascalon}}, an ancient port city in the [[Levant]]}}, borrowed from {{der|en|hbo|אַשְׁקְלוֹן|tr=ʾašqəlôn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[ˈskæ.lɪ.ən]|[ˈskæ.ljn̩]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-scallion.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|now|chiefly|US}} A [[spring onion]], ''[[Allium fistulosum]]''.
# {{lb|en|now|chiefly|US}} Any of various similar members of the [[genus]] ''[[Allium]]''.
# Any onion that lacks a fully developed [[bulb]].
# {{lb|en|US|Scotland}} A [[leek]].

